  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "IR-01",
      "severity": "material linkage issue resolved by explicit proposed construction",
      "status": "Explicit allocation independently checked in memory and in all20 saved monthly day witnesses; original origin preserved.",
      "observation": "The original deterministic allocation assigns employer A CAD145/day and B CAD100/day at the original CAD25 daily fee, and assigns parent B contributions to refundable reserve. Merely equalizing total employer caps does not make expected consumed costs equal.",
      "disposition": "Keep the origin result unchanged. Use an explicit category-specific allocation with all four parents paying CAD40/day to primary care, remaining shared costs split equally, and each employer paying its own CAD10/day worker compensation. At CAD37.50/day fee both employers fund CAD128.75/day.",
      "impact": "The revised allocation matches the economics private-cost formula. Original greedy allocation alone does not support it."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-02",
      "severity": "reporting defect",
      "status": "Requires label correction; frozen primary profit arithmetic unaffected",
      "observation": "minimum_company_cash_cad is updated initially and at month ends, not after every payment. A controlled one-month case reports CAD1588.11 although its intramonth pre-collection trough is CAD1213.11.",
      "disposition": "Label it minimum observed month-end company cash. Do not describe it as a true intramonth minimum or independently established liquidity cushion.",
      "impact": "Cash-outflow guards still preserve the modeled CAD500 reserve; this metric defect does not change modeled profit or policy selection."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-03",
      "severity": "scope/reporting defect",
      "status": "Frozen simulator still assumes closure; separate saved day witnesses support independently derived finite spend/refund identities, not actual external account settlement.",
      "observation": "unsettled_customer_obligations_at_runoff_cad is set to zero as a literal. Customer_pass_funding_separate_cad accumulates maximum proposed pass funding; the simulator does not enumerate external care spending and refunds.",
      "disposition": "Call external zero obligations a scenario closure assumption. A separate monthly ledger can verify spend plus refund equals funded exposure for each declared care scenario.",
      "impact": "Company cash excludes these funds correctly, but that is not an all-participant settlement proof."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-04",
      "severity": "required interpretation",
      "status": "Arithmetic correct; label must state opening finance is included",
      "observation": "available_growth_cash_cad=max(0,closing cash-500) includes remaining opening finance. At the selected policy its mean is CAD6825.3553 versus operating profit CAD4825.3553, a CAD2000 difference.",
      "disposition": "Describe as spendable modeled company cash above reserve, including seed finance, not earned surplus or operating profit.",
      "impact": "No hidden finance is included in profit; the risk is a misleading growth-cash headline."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-05",
      "severity": "accounting boundary",
      "status": "A/B/C coded separately once, subject to stated funding boundary",
      "observation": "A includes launch, attempted work, refusals, acquired leads and active-month overhead once. B assessment CAD120 and historical C planning estimate CAD1100 are subtracted only in a separate after-B-and-C profit field, not in company cash paths. B extraction/invocation/maintenance appear only in prospective retention scenarios because retention is on HOLD.",
      "disposition": "State that opening working finance is available after separately financed or sunk B/C work. If B/C must instead be paid from the same CAD2500, the existing liquidity/wind-down results do not apply unchanged. Actual C is unmetered; CAD1100 is not a complete measured research invoice.",
      "impact": "Coding does not duplicate B/C in A. All-in profitability and cash readiness remain conditional on these scope/funding assumptions."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-06",
      "severity": "conditional-demand limitation",
      "status": "Preserve prominently",
      "observation": "Price selection uses assumed qualified leads, prevented-shift values, contribution margins, confidence, competition haircut, liquidity discount, collective parent participation, eligibility and semantic acceptance. No actual quote, buyer approval, payment or delivered childcare is observed.",
      "disposition": "Call CAD750 a selected simulated policy conditional on these parameters, not a market-validated service price. Report poor outcomes and wind-down alongside the mean.",
      "impact": "Prospective software confirmation can test implementation under fresh random draws; it cannot validate demand or the assumed value distribution."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-07",
      "severity": "buyer-participation scope",
      "status": "Employer individual expected-value check passes; broader participation remains assumed",
      "observation": "Code checks price/2 against the minimum of two employer willingness values, so a high-value employer cannot compensate for a low-value employer automatically. At central parameters each employer needs modeled undiscouted value of about CAD1353.0093. Parent willingness is a collective probability plus fixed caps; workers/providers rely on declared technical consent.",
      "disposition": "Keep employer-specific participation separate from assumed parent/worker/provider acceptance. Require equal per-category funding/refund allocation and actual participant agreement for a real offering.",
      "impact": "Equal full-funding caps are feasible, but caps and solver feasibility are not observed consent or realized benefits."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-08",
      "severity": "unit and horizon boundary",
      "status": "Arithmetic mapping verified; real monthly generalization unproven",
      "observation": "Origin is one synthetic day with a CAD25 coordinator fee. Economics sells twenty repetitions at a CAD750 monthly fee, requiring CAD37.50 per daily equivalent. Daily consumed pass CAD210 plus reserve CAD170 equals CAD380; parent caps imply CAD3200/month and the original CAD70/day fee ceiling implies CAD1400/month.",
      "disposition": "Preserve the origin and label the monthly wrapper as a new explicit transformation. Every repeated day must retain the same constraints or be rechecked; the pre-start single-world outage model does not promise mid-session transfers or simultaneous provider failures.",
      "impact": "The scaled arithmetic is consistent once the new fee and allocation are explicit. It is not evidence of 20 days of actual service."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-09",
      "severity": "cost-model limitation",
      "status": "No additional corrective charge introduced",
      "observation": "Per-attempt A is CAD66.89: inference33.39 + other delivery25.50 + expected recovery8.00. The postaccept correction allowance is charged on every attempt, including rejected ones, which is conservative relative to an acceptance-only event. Actual usage, request sizes, tools, real claims and staffing costs are not metered.",
      "disposition": "Present the unit cost as an assumption at configured prices and keep the complete acquisition/overhead/launch ledger visible. Do not equate CAD66.89 with complete cost per accepted commercial package.",
      "impact": "No actual expenditure or universal cost advantage is established."
    },
    {
      "id": "IR-10",
      "severity": "secondary sensitivity interpretation",
      "status": "Informational; main paired policy selection is unaffected",
      "observation": "All pricing policies share the same stored selection worlds. Some later sensitivity make_world calls regenerate job attributes when a changed beta draw consumes a different number of random numbers; in a 50-index selection-seed audit, changing semantic_acceptance to0.75 changed the job list for1 index.",
      "disposition": "Do not describe those quality sensitivities as exact identical-lead causal experiments. They remain conditional simulations and no operational Alpha is measured. Preserve the zero-gain default.",
      "impact": "This does not alter the already frozen price-family comparison, whose policies use identical world objects."
    }
  ],
